          "question": "Which conditions covered here have a three-character code that takes no further character?",
          "answer": "The following conditions covered here have three-character ICD-10 codes that do not require additional characters:\n\n1. **I10** - This code is for essential, or primary, hypertension and does not take further characters. It falls under Chapter 9, diseases of the circulatory system (source: \"Coding hypertension: I10 and the hypertensive disease family\").\n\n2. **E00** - This code pertains to disorders of the thyroid gland, part of Chapter 4 covering endocrine, nutritional, and metabolic diseases (source: \"ICD-10-CM Chapter 4: endocrine, nutritional and metabolic diseases\").\n\n3. **E07** - This code also falls within Chapter 4 and addresses other disorders of the thyroid gland (source: \"ICD-10-CM Chapter 4: endocrine, nutritional and metabolic diseases\").\n\n4. **E08** - This code is used for diabetes mellitus due to an underlying condition (source: \"ICD-10-CM Chapter 4: endocrine, nutritional and metabolic diseases\").\n\n5. **E11** - This code is for type 2 diabetes mellitus and defaults to this category when no type is specified (source: \"Coding type 2 diabetes: E11 and its complication subcategories\").\n\n6. **E89** - This code covers specific postprocedural states and does not require further specificity (source: \"ICD-10-CM Chapter 4: endocrine, nutritional and metabolic diseases\").\n\nThis information is based on the ICD-10 coding conventions and clarifications provided in the retrieved sources. If you need more details about any specific condition or coding practices, please let me know!\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
